# Milestone: M3
# Covers: real-time priority (tag.setPriority(5)) causes high-priority strand to
#         run without interruption; loop counter stays at 0 relative to origin.
# defer-to: never (requires URBI_SCHED_RT real-time scheduler — v1.x only)
#
# Reason:
#   This fixture tests real-time scheduling priorities via tag.setPriority(n),
#   which requires URBI_SCHED_RT — the real-time scheduler variant that is v1.x
#   scope (post-v1.0 freestanding milestone).  The cooperative scheduler used
#   through v1.0 does not implement priority preemption.  REVIVAL.md §12 marks
#   URBI_SCHED_RT as v1.x scope.  Also uses tag.setPriority() and tag.stop()
#   method dispatch (M4), and ',' separator (M5 chk driver).
#
# Original urbiscript (activate at v1.x with URBI_SCHED_RT):
# # var x = 0 | {};
# # t: { while(true) x++ },
# # var hp = Tag.new() | hp.setPriority(5) | {};
# # hp: { var xorig = x; for(var i: 100) nil; x - xorig };
# # [00000001] 0
# # t.stop();
